OL,3,GNEWSAApology after two women's rights
OL,4,Acampaigners banned
OL,5,
OL,6,FBristol City Council has apologised
OL,7,F"unreservedly" and agreed to pay some
OL,8,Flegal costs after two gender critical
OL,9,Fcampaigners were banned from the
OL,10,Fchamber.
OL,12,FPhoebe Beedell and Wendy Stephenson
OL,13,Fwere excluded from public meetings for
OL,14,Fsix months, after the authority said
OL,15,Ftheir conduct led to some councillors
OL,16,Ffeeling "intimidated".
OL,18,FThe women launched a legal challenge,
OL,19,Fand now the council has agreed to
OL,20,Fsettle the dispute out of court.
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
